  "id": "COMPOUND:21337 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "Neridienone A is shown to have a target relationship with SNU-387, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol, (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, and S-ethylcysteine zwitterion. All these compounds are linked to HepG2, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Neridienone A may exert its effects on this cell line. The evidence points to a pathway where Neridienone A targets SNU-387, which is a common target of multiple compounds, and these compounds in turn target HepG2. This implies that the interaction between Neridienone A and HepG2 may involve a shared target or a downstream effect mediated through SNU-387. The evidence supports a possible role for Neridienone A in modulating HepG2 through its interaction with SNU-387, which is a key intermediate in the targeting process.",
